# oif bench profile "poisson" (B-4a): open loop for Qwen3-0.6B. The levels are requests per second with Poisson
# arrivals, not users: no waves of requests that end and restart together (the closed loop's p50 TTFT depends on them,
# B-3a evidence 00 and 03). 4, 8 and 12 requests/s are about 25-70% of what plain vLLM serves on the W7900 (chat at
# 64 users: 17 requests/s); the A6000 gets the same offered load. chat is the shape of the B-1b/B-2 posts, d256 and p1k
# the B-3a shapes where Dynamo's TTFT p99 was lower. Prefix cache off as in B-3a.
BENCH_ARRIVAL=poisson
BENCH_WORKLOADS="chat:512:256 d256:128:256 p1k:1024:16"
BENCH_CONCURRENCY="4 8 12"
BENCH_DURATION_S=120
BENCH_REPEATS=1
BENCH_PREFIX_CACHE=off
